.TH BYTE_SKIPN 3
.SH NAME
byte_skipn \- count the run of bytes other than a given byte at the start of a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t byte_skipn(const void* " p ", size_t " n ", char " c ");
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_skipn
returns the number of consecutive bytes not equal to c at the start of p.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The run length; if c does not occur at all, it returns n.
.PP
These are the single-byte counterparts of the scan_charset*skip functions.
byte_skipn is a macro for byte_chr.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_chr (3),
.BR byte_rskipn (3)
